WEBVTT

1
00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:18.906
Strange.

2
00:03:19.824 --> 00:03:21.992
Who'd do something like this?

3
00:03:23.578 --> 00:03:26.413
Maybe someone got a little upset
about their roaming charges.

4
00:03:27.415 --> 00:03:31.084
Stealing satellite phones
makes sense. You can hock them.

5
00:03:31.669 --> 00:03:35.047
You can run up charges
on somebody else's account.

6
00:03:35.757 --> 00:03:37.674
But burning them?

7
00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:39.676
Youngsters?

8
00:03:39.844 --> 00:03:41.720
Pulling some prank?

9
00:03:42.138 --> 00:03:43.597
No.

10
00:03:44.265 --> 00:03:46.308
They'd have left a note.

11
00:03:46.768 --> 00:03:49.228
"Fuck you" to their parents...

12
00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.939
...or the world or whatever.

13
00:03:58.363 --> 00:04:00.405
Not a bad idea, though.

14
00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:20.133
I brought Peggy here
on our first date.

15
00:04:20.301 --> 00:04:22.261
Yeah, we all did.

16
00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.723
Not Peggy, of course.

17
00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.811
Yeah, I got you.

18
00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:36.441
Last sunset in a month...

19
00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.068
...always works.

20
00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.742
Come on. Let's go do the sign.

21
00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:50.664
You okay, Eben?

22
00:04:53.418 --> 00:04:55.002
Yeah.

23
00:05:33.416 --> 00:05:36.626
Why do you even bother with that?
Nobody's gonna see it for a month.

24
00:05:36.794 --> 00:05:38.128
It's tradition.

25
00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:00.150
Put this off till the last minute,
didn't you?

26
00:06:00.318 --> 00:06:03.028
There's a lot of small towns
in this state.

27
00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:07.074
My boss wants all his gear inspected
and certified by the 31st.

28
00:06:08.076 --> 00:06:10.285
And I noticed you saved
Barrow for the last.

29
00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:15.207
You sure you don't wanna stay?

30
00:06:15.625 --> 00:06:17.667
Me and Jeannie were hoping
you and Eben...

31
00:06:17.835 --> 00:06:21.421
...might rethink
this separation thing.

32
00:06:23.925 --> 00:06:25.592
Thanks.

33
00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:27.469
I...

34
00:06:28.346 --> 00:06:30.305
...gotta make the plane.

35
00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:42.567
Okay, sweetie. I know you can't
handle a month with no sun.

36
00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:45.695
I promise I won't live on
Oreos and Snapple, all right?

37
00:06:51.702 --> 00:06:52.869
Have fun in Seattle.

38
00:06:53.037 --> 00:06:57.707
Yeah. So long, Kirsten.
I'll call you when I get there.

39
00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:00.961
Goodbye.

40
00:07:41.169 --> 00:07:43.003
Got a problem?

41
00:07:44.881 --> 00:07:47.340
Nothing I can't handle
my own fucking self.

42
00:07:53.389 --> 00:07:55.307
This for generators?

43
00:07:57.727 --> 00:07:59.853
Yeah. Yeah, mostly.

44
00:08:01.022 --> 00:08:04.357
Beau, I have to cite you for it.
I can't have it leaking on the street.

45
00:08:07.528 --> 00:08:09.237
What?

46
00:08:12.033 --> 00:08:13.742
For that? You don't...

47
00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:17.913
You don't have to cite me.

48
00:08:18.456 --> 00:08:20.999
You don't have to do anything.

49
00:08:23.044 --> 00:08:26.129
Isn't that why we live out here?

50
00:08:26.547 --> 00:08:28.965
You know, for a little freedom?

51
00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:32.636
Happy motoring.

52
00:08:38.392 --> 00:08:40.894
Yeah, I'll add it to my collection.

53
00:08:44.106 --> 00:08:47.567
You know, Beau's not so bad.
Why'd you bother writing him up?

54
00:08:48.569 --> 00:08:51.863
He lives all alone out there
on the south ridge.

55
00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:56.201
A little citation now and then
lets him know he's a part of this town.

56
00:08:57.662 --> 00:09:00.247
Eben? Come in, Eben.

57
00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:03.750
Yeah, Helen.

58
00:09:03.918 --> 00:09:07.087
Something bad's happened
to John Riis' dogs.

59
00:09:15.054 --> 00:09:18.974
Well, folks, you're listening
to KBRW, Barrow, Alaska.

60
00:09:19.141 --> 00:09:20.267
Today's the last day...

61
00:09:23.187 --> 00:09:26.106
I'm leaving too, getting
on that last plane out of here.

62
00:09:48.796 --> 00:09:50.046
Hey, Stella, are you okay?

63
00:09:53.217 --> 00:09:55.468
Damn it, Malekai.

64
00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:58.555
Don't you know what
"right of way" means?

65
00:09:58.723 --> 00:10:00.140
I'm sorry, Stella.

66
00:10:00.641 --> 00:10:02.350
The brakes jammed and...

67
00:10:02.518 --> 00:10:05.854
Eben wanted this back from the airport
before the storm hit, and I was...

68
00:10:06.022 --> 00:10:09.149
Oh, shit.
Who's gonna run me to the airport?

69
00:10:09.859 --> 00:10:11.651
Well, wouldn't Eben?

70
00:10:13.362 --> 00:10:15.572
My mom could come down
and give you a tow...

71
00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:18.074
...but, you know,
she don't move too fast.

72
00:10:18.826 --> 00:10:20.243
Fuck! Where's my phone?

73
00:10:48.105 --> 00:10:49.147
It's me.

74
00:10:49.774 --> 00:10:51.691
Surprise.

75
00:10:55.446 --> 00:10:58.365
I... I need a ride to the airport.

76
00:10:58.866 --> 00:11:00.408
What?

77
00:11:01.869 --> 00:11:04.287
You're in town,
and you didn't wanna talk?

78
00:11:04.455 --> 00:11:09.542
I had fire-marshal work here,
and I just had a little accident.

79
00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:12.087
I'm stuck on Ransom and 355.
The airport'll close...

80
00:11:12.254 --> 00:11:14.422
...and I'll never get to Anchorage.

81
00:11:18.886 --> 00:11:22.013
I mean, if you wanna talk,
we can do it on the drive.

82
00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:27.936
Hey, Billy.

83
00:11:28.104 --> 00:11:30.105
Stella's stuck at Ransom and 355.

84
00:11:30.272 --> 00:11:33.149
She needs a ride to the airport.
Can you go get her?

85
00:11:38.239 --> 00:11:39.739
Yeah.

86
00:11:40.324 --> 00:11:42.158
John Riis needs me for something...

87
00:11:42.326 --> 00:11:44.452
...so Billy's gonna come get you.

88
00:11:46.414 --> 00:11:48.707
Let me know if a day comes
when you do wanna talk.

89
00:12:19.739 --> 00:12:22.115
What sick jerk would do this?

90
00:12:22.283 --> 00:12:26.035
Every kennel. Every dog we had.

91
00:12:26.495 --> 00:12:28.997
Did you fight with anyone
recently, John?

92
00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:36.296
I'll kill them. I'll kill them.

93
00:12:38.132 --> 00:12:39.632
This wasn't done long ago.

94
00:12:41.886 --> 00:12:45.430
I'll find them. Okay?

95
00:12:52.313 --> 00:12:53.605
You'll be okay, Malekai.

96
00:12:58.986 --> 00:13:02.280
- Where have you been?
- I couldn't find the damn car keys.

97
00:13:02.448 --> 00:13:06.701
Then I was like, "Wait, was that
Rogers and 355 or Ransom?"

98
00:13:06.869 --> 00:13:08.995
- And then...
- Yeah, never mind. Let's go.

99
00:13:13.375 --> 00:13:15.960
It would be a lot easier
if you just played, Grandma.

100
00:13:16.128 --> 00:13:20.507
Oh, I don't really care for those sort of
games, if you wanna know the truth.

101
00:13:22.009 --> 00:13:23.510
Try your brother.

102
00:13:25.387 --> 00:13:27.806
- What?
- Eben, do you wanna play?

103
00:13:29.225 --> 00:13:31.518
I can't right now, Jake. Sorry.

104
00:13:32.102 --> 00:13:35.021
While you were busy with John Riis,
Carter and Wilson called...

105
00:13:35.189 --> 00:13:37.899
...about a vandalism problem
at the Utilidor.

106
00:13:41.111 --> 00:13:42.570
Thanks.

107
00:13:45.199 --> 00:13:48.660
Call Point Hope and Wainwright.
See if they're having any troubles.

108
00:14:03.717 --> 00:14:05.218
No.

109
00:14:07.888 --> 00:14:11.057
I am not trapped here for a month.

110
00:14:19.149 --> 00:14:22.068
- There's someone you can bunk with.
- Don't start, Billy.

111
00:14:22.236 --> 00:14:26.030
Peggy and me can put two girls in one
room. You'd have a place of your own.

112
00:14:26.198 --> 00:14:29.742
I can't stay here. I've got bills
to put in the mail. My plants'll die.

113
00:14:30.703 --> 00:14:31.995
It'll all work out.

114
00:14:33.205 --> 00:14:35.415
Of course, the price
of staying at my place...

115
00:14:35.583 --> 00:14:39.127
...is explaining to me and Peggy
just what is wrong with you and Eben.

116
00:14:44.884 --> 00:14:48.344
Not enough time this century
to cover that, Billy.

117
00:15:14.371 --> 00:15:15.872
Eben, how you doing?

118
00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:17.582
- Good to see you.
- Hey, Carter.

119
00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.626
Lord, it's gotta be 10 below out here.

120
00:15:19.793 --> 00:15:21.961
- Eben.
- Wilson.

121
00:15:30.095 --> 00:15:32.680
Can't your wife bring you up
a sweater or two?

122
00:15:33.641 --> 00:15:35.683
Bring the whole tribe up
while she's at it?

123
00:15:36.977 --> 00:15:38.937
They'll come when they're ready,
I guess.

124
00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:40.813
So...

125
00:15:40.981 --> 00:15:44.609
...I've found all kinds of garbage
in here over the years.

126
00:15:44.777 --> 00:15:46.986
Blue jeans, bikes...

127
00:15:47.154 --> 00:15:50.657
Sometimes I can yank them out before
the muffin monster chews them to shit.

128
00:15:50.824 --> 00:15:52.784
The muffin monster?

129
00:16:01.126 --> 00:16:02.710
I saw Wilson's helicopter logo.

130
00:16:02.878 --> 00:16:05.296
Pulled that stuff out
before it got totally trashed.

131
00:16:10.302 --> 00:16:12.762
You keep your copter
under lock and key, don't you?

132
00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:16.599
Yeah, I put it in dry dock
when the tourists headed south.

133
00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:19.936
I haven't looked at it for days.
They ripped out the throttle...

134
00:16:20.104 --> 00:16:22.689
...the rotors,
half the fucking helicopter!

135
00:16:22.982 --> 00:16:24.607
It's my life, Eben.

136
00:16:25.734 --> 00:16:28.569
Why would someone
rip the hell out of my bird?

137
00:18:00.454 --> 00:18:02.121
Hey! Stop!

138
00:18:03.874 --> 00:18:05.708
Stop! Stop!

139
00:18:06.168 --> 00:18:07.251
Who are you people?

140
00:18:23.393 --> 00:18:25.269
No whiskey?

141
00:18:25.813 --> 00:18:27.522
No rum?

142
00:18:27.689 --> 00:18:29.440
Alcohol's illegal this month.

143
00:18:30.984 --> 00:18:34.403
Folks have a hard enough time in the
dark without booze making it worse.

144
00:18:36.156 --> 00:18:39.325
Well, forget about the liquor...

145
00:18:39.618 --> 00:18:41.327
...Lucy.

146
00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:44.122
Just bring me a bowl of...

147
00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:47.166
...raw hamburger.

148
00:18:47.334 --> 00:18:51.504
You can only get meat two ways
around here, frozen or burnt.

149
00:18:54.216 --> 00:18:58.052
You don't bring me what I wanna eat,
what I wanna drink.

150
00:18:58.220 --> 00:19:00.304
That's enough, pal.

151
00:19:00.681 --> 00:19:02.598
Leave the lady be.

152
00:19:25.873 --> 00:19:29.542
Hey, what do you say the two of us
go outside and have a little talk, huh?

153
00:19:31.086 --> 00:19:36.716
Well, now, what's wrong with a man
wanting a little fresh meat?

154
00:19:39.887 --> 00:19:41.846
Come on. You and me, let's go.

155
00:19:45.392 --> 00:19:47.185
I'm taking you outside.

156
00:19:47.352 --> 00:19:49.562
I would like to see that.

157
00:19:52.065 --> 00:19:54.025
I would too.

158
00:19:54.818 --> 00:19:58.738
But then Lucy'd have to clean up
after Eben kicked your ass.

159
00:20:02.618 --> 00:20:05.161
It's more trouble than you're worth.

160
00:20:11.335 --> 00:20:13.169
Hey, be nice!

161
00:20:15.756 --> 00:20:17.256
Enough.

162
00:20:17.424 --> 00:20:18.925
Stay down.

163
00:20:22.304 --> 00:20:24.931
Fire marshal's office lets you carry
one of those things?

164
00:20:25.098 --> 00:20:28.476
It's a funny thing, I never asked.

165
00:20:30.103 --> 00:20:31.270
So you missed your flight?

166
00:20:31.438 --> 00:20:34.440
That sucks. Where you gonna stay?

167
00:20:39.279 --> 00:20:43.241
Billy and Peggy are putting me up.

168
00:20:47.287 --> 00:20:49.956
Well, I'll talk to you sometime,
I guess.

169
00:20:53.293 --> 00:20:54.627
Hey, listen.

170
00:20:55.796 --> 00:20:59.924
Look, maybe I'll come along
and say hi to Jake and Helen.

171
00:21:04.096 --> 00:21:05.596
Bye, Luce.

172
00:21:14.773 --> 00:21:18.025
We haven't seen vandalism
like this in a long time.

173
00:21:18.860 --> 00:21:22.029
Don't you know how to take care
of this town without me?

174
00:21:32.165 --> 00:21:34.667
Malekai totaled my car.

175
00:21:35.419 --> 00:21:37.420
Hell of a day.

176
00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:39.672
Just you wait.

177
00:21:55.856 --> 00:21:57.648
Hey, Jake.

178
00:22:04.281 --> 00:22:07.241
- Where are we going?
- I'm heading back to your house.

179
00:22:07.409 --> 00:22:08.451
My landlady...

180
00:22:08.618 --> 00:22:11.370
...doesn't want pipeline workers
keeping her up all night.

181
00:22:11.538 --> 00:22:13.164
Denise is right.

182
00:22:13.373 --> 00:22:16.834
- Let's head back to my place.
- Neither of you are getting me alone.

183
00:22:17.002 --> 00:22:18.586
Neither!

184
00:22:18.920 --> 00:22:22.214
We share, right?
None of us have to be greedy.

185
00:22:22.382 --> 00:22:26.052
- Yeah, come on. We'll be good.
- Oh, you will?

186
00:22:26.219 --> 00:22:29.847
- Where's the fun in that, Gabe?
- You bad little bitch.

187
00:22:30.015 --> 00:22:31.891
All right, all right,
Rock, Paper, Scissors.

188
00:22:32.225 --> 00:22:35.519
- Whoever wins, we go to his place.
- Good idea. Let's do it.

189
00:22:35.687 --> 00:22:37.563
- Come on.
- Hurry up, let's get moving.

190
00:22:38.315 --> 00:22:40.024
On three.

191
00:22:40.734 --> 00:22:42.193
One, two...

192
00:22:45.447 --> 00:22:50.951
Gabe?

193
00:22:51.745 --> 00:22:52.912
Gabe!

194
00:23:13.141 --> 00:23:15.351
Let me tell you what I got.

195
00:23:16.561 --> 00:23:18.562
You don't work at the refinery.

196
00:23:19.439 --> 00:23:23.025
You didn't fly in.
Somebody'd have seen you.

197
00:23:23.944 --> 00:23:26.695
And you're definitely
not from around here.

198
00:23:26.863 --> 00:23:28.864
How'd you get in?

199
00:23:37.165 --> 00:23:38.707
All right.

200
00:23:41.253 --> 00:23:45.423
We got a long time to figure this out.
Nobody's coming for you for a month.

201
00:24:03.650 --> 00:24:06.152
Jake, come here a second.

202
00:24:13.493 --> 00:24:15.453
What the hell is that?

203
00:24:15.787 --> 00:24:19.832
It's pot. It helps her with her cancer.

204
00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:23.836
Didn't tell you I got a little greenhouse
at home. Didn't want you arresting me.

205
00:24:26.798 --> 00:24:29.008
Now I know why you wanted
to live with Grandma.

206
00:24:29.176 --> 00:24:31.969
No, I just thought you and Stella
ought to have some privacy.

207
00:24:32.137 --> 00:24:34.013
Well, that worked out.

208
00:24:36.433 --> 00:24:38.350
Computer's down.

209
00:24:40.645 --> 00:24:42.396
I'll call Gus.

210
00:24:47.027 --> 00:24:49.195
Strange.

211
00:24:50.655 --> 00:24:52.656
The phone's down too.

212
00:24:52.824 --> 00:24:56.285
Mr. and Mrs. Sheriff.

213
00:24:56.912 --> 00:24:59.538
So sweet.

214
00:24:59.748 --> 00:25:01.499
So...

215
00:25:01.666 --> 00:25:05.669
...helpless against what is coming.

216
00:25:07.547 --> 00:25:09.965
He's just trying to freak us out.

217
00:25:11.009 --> 00:25:12.176
It's working.

218
00:25:13.929 --> 00:25:16.388
We have more important things
to think about.

219
00:25:16.806 --> 00:25:19.725
- I'll check on Gus.
- Check on Gus.

220
00:25:20.352 --> 00:25:22.394
Bar the windows.

221
00:25:22.562 --> 00:25:24.396
Try to hide.

222
00:25:24.856 --> 00:25:26.732
They're coming.

223
00:25:28.235 --> 00:25:32.738
This time they gonna
take me with them, honor me.

224
00:25:33.573 --> 00:25:37.409
Yeah. For all that I have done.

225
00:25:38.411 --> 00:25:39.995
"They"?

226
00:25:44.251 --> 00:25:45.376
Who are "they"?

227
00:25:57.180 --> 00:25:59.431
The generator's kicked in.

228
00:26:15.782 --> 00:26:19.076
- I'm heading out to the cell tower.
- We have to stay here with him?

229
00:26:19.703 --> 00:26:22.538
Sure. We'll keep an eye on him.

230
00:26:23.081 --> 00:26:25.791
As soon as the lines are back up,
get Billy over here.

231
00:26:25.959 --> 00:26:28.836
Stay on the walkie-talkie with me
until the power's back.

232
00:26:50.150 --> 00:26:51.650
Gus!

233
00:27:02.078 --> 00:27:03.495
Gus?

234
00:27:34.861 --> 00:27:39.698
This is Sheriff Eben Oleson.
Stay in your homes, lock your doors...

235
00:27:40.075 --> 00:27:43.035
...and load your firearms.
This is not a drill.

236
00:27:44.496 --> 00:27:47.039
- Is your genny up and running?
- Yeah.

237
00:27:47.791 --> 00:27:51.168
Anyone with a genny should go home
immediately, just to be safe.

238
00:27:51.336 --> 00:27:53.796
If you don't have one,
you should meet at the diner.

239
00:27:53.963 --> 00:27:56.799
I heard gunshots, Eben.
What the hell is going on?

240
00:27:57.050 --> 00:27:58.634
I don't know.

241
00:28:00.970 --> 00:28:03.889
Just go home.
I'll let you know when I find out, okay?

242
00:28:04.057 --> 00:28:05.224
Okay.

243
00:28:08.645 --> 00:28:10.562
Come on, guys. Let's go.

244
00:28:17.821 --> 00:28:19.405
Let's just have dinner, John.

245
00:28:23.618 --> 00:28:25.160
Please?

246
00:28:46.433 --> 00:28:48.809
John! John!

247
00:28:49.060 --> 00:28:50.269
- Ally!
- John!

248
00:28:51.062 --> 00:28:53.355
No! No! John!

249
00:28:56.526 --> 00:29:08.370
John!

250
00:29:08.538 --> 00:29:10.497
No!

251
00:29:12.959 --> 00:29:14.626
John!

252
00:29:14.794 --> 00:29:16.378
Ally! Ally!

253
00:29:17.714 --> 00:29:20.048
- John! John!
- Ally!

254
00:29:20.216 --> 00:29:21.425
- Oh, my God!
- Ally!

255
00:29:21.593 --> 00:29:24.344
- John! John!
- Ally!

256
00:29:24.512 --> 00:29:27.598
Oh, my God. No!

257
00:29:30.351 --> 00:29:32.478
No way out of town.

258
00:29:33.271 --> 00:29:34.813
No one to come help.

259
00:29:34.981 --> 00:29:37.024
- Shut up.
- Ignore him, Jake.

260
00:29:38.693 --> 00:29:40.319
You can feel it.

261
00:29:41.988 --> 00:29:47.117
That cold ain't the weather,
that's death approaching.

262
00:29:49.496 --> 00:29:51.955
Who you think they gonna take first?

263
00:29:53.875 --> 00:29:58.629
The girl who thinks
a gun will help her?

264
00:29:58.963 --> 00:30:02.090
The kid, sheriff's kid?
Or the old gal?

265
00:30:02.342 --> 00:30:04.051
Shut up!

266
00:30:07.972 --> 00:30:09.139
Yeah.

267
00:30:10.350 --> 00:30:13.018
Thank you for the plastique.

268
00:30:13.186 --> 00:30:17.397
I can snap that apart
and pick the lock.

269
00:30:17.565 --> 00:30:20.692
- No, you won't.
- Jake, he can't. Jake.

270
00:30:22.862 --> 00:30:24.071
Jake.

271
00:30:34.207 --> 00:30:35.999
You shithead.

272
00:30:37.293 --> 00:30:39.044
Helen, get the first-aid kit.

273
00:30:50.807 --> 00:30:55.018
All right, time to talk.
Who are you here with?

274
00:30:55.353 --> 00:30:56.812
Who are you here with?

275
00:31:00.400 --> 00:31:02.734
Who did that to Gus?

276
00:31:04.904 --> 00:31:07.239
You're a dead man.

277
00:31:07.615 --> 00:31:09.533
Where are they?!

278
00:31:10.577 --> 00:31:12.995
I don't talk to dead men.

279
00:31:13.788 --> 00:31:16.498
I don't talk to dead men!

280
00:31:19.127 --> 00:31:21.753
Well, if I'm dead,
no one lets you loose from here.

281
00:31:22.213 --> 00:31:24.256
You're all dead!

282
00:31:32.432 --> 00:31:34.766
I can take care of that for now,
but Doc Miller...

283
00:31:34.934 --> 00:31:38.687
No. Wait till the power's back.
Call Doc Miller then.

284
00:31:38.938 --> 00:31:41.523
This fucker doesn't deserve
anything till then.

285
00:31:48.031 --> 00:31:53.118
Billy and I'll work our way
from South Street to the pipeline.

286
00:31:55.538 --> 00:31:58.457
His friends don't have
many places to hide.

287
00:31:59.250 --> 00:32:01.126
I'll join you.

288
00:32:02.086 --> 00:32:03.462
No, we got it.

289
00:32:05.798 --> 00:32:08.675
Right now, you, me and Billy
are the authorities.

290
00:32:08.843 --> 00:32:11.470
It'd be stupid not to take more help.

291
00:32:11.638 --> 00:32:14.514
We got walkie-talkies. We'll be fine.

292
00:32:17.185 --> 00:32:20.646
There's a Taser in the back.
If he gives you any trouble...

293
00:32:20.813 --> 00:32:23.315
...use it. Okay?

294
00:32:23.733 --> 00:32:26.026
You drive. I'm riding shotgun.

295
00:32:31.699 --> 00:32:34.284
- Stop the truck.
- What?

296
00:32:34.661 --> 00:32:35.827
Stop the fucking truck.

297
00:32:48.758 --> 00:32:50.509
I thought I saw something.

298
00:33:03.773 --> 00:33:05.190
- Get in the truck.
- What?

299
00:33:05.692 --> 00:33:06.900
Get in the fucking truck!

300
00:33:20.331 --> 00:33:21.915
- Jesus Christ!
- Fuck!

301
00:33:31.009 --> 00:33:32.551
- Holy shit!
- Fuck!

302
00:33:44.647 --> 00:33:46.231
What the hell was that?

303
00:34:02.540 --> 00:34:05.500
Shit! What was that?
Where was that? Where was that?

304
00:34:06.252 --> 00:34:08.045
No!

305
00:34:08.296 --> 00:34:09.504
- Helen!
- Help!

306
00:34:09.672 --> 00:34:12.591
Helen! Helen, come in!

307
00:34:20.266 --> 00:34:21.391
Jake?

308
00:34:21.934 --> 00:34:22.934
Helen?

309
00:34:24.812 --> 00:34:26.146
Are you here?

310
00:34:29.150 --> 00:34:30.942
Oh, shit.

311
00:34:43.873 --> 00:34:47.292
They didn't take me.

312
00:34:53.633 --> 00:34:55.592
Who did they take?

313
00:34:56.552 --> 00:34:59.429
They didn't take me.

314
00:35:05.144 --> 00:35:07.270
Did they take my brother?

315
00:35:20.326 --> 00:35:22.202
Finish me off.

316
00:35:27.125 --> 00:35:29.084
Finish me.

317
00:35:32.338 --> 00:35:33.797
Eben.

318
00:35:35.675 --> 00:35:37.676
Eben, look at me.

319
00:35:39.011 --> 00:35:40.679
No.

320
00:35:58.156 --> 00:36:05.203
The heads must be separated
from the bodies.

321
00:36:06.789 --> 00:36:08.707
Do not turn them.

322
00:36:14.338 --> 00:36:18.049
We should have come here ages ago.

323
00:36:43.576 --> 00:36:45.452
What are they?

324
00:36:48.581 --> 00:36:50.373
We don't know.

325
00:36:50.541 --> 00:36:54.419
- Wilson, I wanna go home.
- It's okay. Dad!

326
00:36:54.587 --> 00:36:57.756
- It's okay.
- You keep shooting and they just...

327
00:36:58.216 --> 00:36:59.633
They just keep coming.

328
00:36:59.842 --> 00:37:02.761
- How is that possible?
- I don't know.

329
00:37:02.929 --> 00:37:05.972
Maybe they're all coked up
on PCP or something, you know.

330
00:37:06.140 --> 00:37:08.266
They don't feel any bullets.

331
00:37:15.149 --> 00:37:17.651
They killed every sled dog in town.

332
00:37:20.988 --> 00:37:23.281
They took Aaron and Gabe.

333
00:37:23.449 --> 00:37:25.116
They killed my grandmother.

334
00:37:51.727 --> 00:37:54.396
There is no escape.

335
00:37:55.690 --> 00:37:58.149
No hope.

336
00:37:59.110 --> 00:38:01.778
Only hunger and pain.

337
00:39:05.676 --> 00:39:08.553
What are you? What are you?

338
00:40:10.408 --> 00:40:13.576
- Lucy, is the back door locked? Okay.
- All locked.

339
00:40:15.538 --> 00:40:17.122
Jake?

340
00:40:18.791 --> 00:40:22.001
- Eben! Eben!
- Jake.

341
00:40:23.504 --> 00:40:26.965
- Who the hell are these people, Eben?
- What do they want?

342
00:40:32.596 --> 00:40:35.432
We'll figure that out when we
get you guys someplace safe.

343
00:40:35.599 --> 00:40:38.852
There's a generator at the Utilidor.

344
00:40:39.019 --> 00:40:42.814
No, that's way out on the edge of town.
We need someplace close to hide.

345
00:40:42.982 --> 00:40:43.982
Now.

346
00:40:46.360 --> 00:40:48.278
Charlie Kelso's attic.

347
00:40:48.988 --> 00:40:51.489
It has a pull-down ladder.
You can't tell it's there.

348
00:40:52.324 --> 00:40:54.826
He would've boarded up
his home before he left.

349
00:40:55.369 --> 00:40:57.287
Which is exactly why it's a good idea.

350
00:40:57.746 --> 00:41:00.957
We'll pull down a board to get in,
then we'll tack it back.

351
00:41:01.459 --> 00:41:02.709
Carter.

352
00:41:07.047 --> 00:41:09.591
I want you to lead everybody
close to the buildings.

353
00:41:09.758 --> 00:41:11.968
If you hear anything,
roll under a crawlspace.

354
00:41:12.136 --> 00:41:15.722
Go straight to Kelso's attic.
I'll meet you there.

355
00:41:16.056 --> 00:41:17.891
What are you gonna do?

356
00:41:20.478 --> 00:41:24.355
I'm gonna load up with as many bear
traps and flares as a 4x4 can carry.

357
00:41:24.857 --> 00:41:27.150
Something's gotta slow them down.

358
00:41:32.907 --> 00:41:34.324
I'm coming with you.

359
00:41:36.869 --> 00:41:37.911
Okay.

360
00:42:03.479 --> 00:42:04.729
- Fuck!
- Oh, shit!

361
00:42:05.231 --> 00:42:06.231
Shit!

362
00:42:13.822 --> 00:42:15.323
Fuck!

363
00:42:17.743 --> 00:42:19.118
Shit!

364
00:42:34.301 --> 00:42:36.094
Eben!

365
00:42:38.847 --> 00:42:40.515
No!

366
00:42:45.771 --> 00:42:47.063
Go! Get out of here!

367
00:42:49.024 --> 00:42:50.608
Shit. Shit. Shit.

368
00:42:58.242 --> 00:42:59.784
Move it. Move it!

369
00:43:01.745 --> 00:43:03.288
Come on!

370
00:43:11.964 --> 00:43:13.381
Go!

371
00:43:19.805 --> 00:43:21.973
- What the hell is going on?
- I don't know.

372
00:43:22.141 --> 00:43:25.184
- We gotta lose this thing.
- And go where?

373
00:43:25.811 --> 00:43:27.687
We know a place.

374
00:43:44.371 --> 00:43:45.872
Okay.

375
00:43:57.468 --> 00:43:58.801
Go.

376
00:44:18.989 --> 00:44:20.990
These seem to work.

377
00:44:24.578 --> 00:44:25.953
It's well hidden.

378
00:44:39.343 --> 00:44:40.718
Hey.

379
00:44:47.559 --> 00:44:49.560
Two, three.

380
00:45:25.723 --> 00:45:27.640
I saw them...

381
00:45:29.101 --> 00:45:31.894
...feed on Grandma Helen.

382
00:45:33.689 --> 00:45:37.066
They're like vampires, you know?

383
00:45:39.194 --> 00:45:41.112
Vampires don't exist, Jake.

384
00:45:42.156 --> 00:45:44.240
They don't fall when you shoot them.

385
00:45:45.075 --> 00:45:46.534
Hell, neither do I.

386
00:45:47.369 --> 00:45:51.038
Well, I don't care what they are.
I just care what we do about them.

387
00:45:52.124 --> 00:45:54.417
What are we gonna do about them?

388
00:45:58.505 --> 00:46:00.590
We'll sleep in shifts.

389
00:46:02.259 --> 00:46:06.012
We'll ration our food, and then
we'll figure out the next step.

390
00:46:08.557 --> 00:46:12.268
We have two advantages.
We know this town...

391
00:46:12.978 --> 00:46:14.270
...and we know the cold.

392
00:46:15.481 --> 00:46:17.148
We live here for a reason.

393
00:46:19.234 --> 00:46:21.444
Because nobody else can.

394
00:46:29.161 --> 00:46:31.204
Yeah, right.

395
00:46:52.935 --> 00:46:58.147
You did all that I asked.

396
00:47:06.406 --> 00:47:10.535
We will take care of you.

397
00:47:34.768 --> 00:47:39.063
The things they believe.

398
00:47:59.585 --> 00:48:02.336
I guess it's good
you didn't want kids, huh?

399
00:48:03.630 --> 00:48:05.423
Imagine.

400
00:48:08.176 --> 00:48:10.511
Where... ? Where's Catherine?
Where's Catherine?

401
00:48:10.679 --> 00:48:13.097
- Dad. Dad. Dad.
- What?

402
00:48:13.265 --> 00:48:16.601
Dad, Mom died a long time ago.

403
00:48:19.104 --> 00:48:20.354
Isaac...

404
00:48:20.522 --> 00:48:24.901
...you should go to sleep now.
You should go to sleep.

405
00:48:25.319 --> 00:48:29.363
That's right. That's right.
You should go to sleep.

406
00:48:32.117 --> 00:48:33.868
Thank you.

407
00:48:51.845 --> 00:48:54.388
They're ransacking the Clarks' place.

408
00:48:55.223 --> 00:48:57.141
They're tearing through
everyone's home.

409
00:48:57.392 --> 00:49:00.853
- We have to move.
- When do you suggest we do that?

410
00:49:01.313 --> 00:49:04.273
Now, while we have the strength.

411
00:49:04.983 --> 00:49:08.277
Until we have some way to stop them,
it's suicide, Lucy.

412
00:49:08.445 --> 00:49:11.072
We can stay here until they find us...

413
00:49:11.239 --> 00:49:13.282
...and they can kill us all,
or we can run.

414
00:49:13.450 --> 00:49:16.077
Some won't make it,
but it's better than all of us dying!

415
00:49:16.244 --> 00:49:18.079
- Shut up!
- Doug, you should sit down.

416
00:49:18.288 --> 00:49:19.580
Maybe Denise or Lucy dies...

417
00:49:19.748 --> 00:49:22.083
...but that's okay so long as
you have a chance?

418
00:49:22.250 --> 00:49:24.335
- Hey. Hey.
- Hey.

419
00:49:32.344 --> 00:49:33.594
Stupid.

420
00:49:40.852 --> 00:49:44.689
Start a fight, that'll get us all
killed a lot faster.

421
00:49:55.701 --> 00:49:56.826
Okay.

422
00:50:01.873 --> 00:50:05.626
We go to the general store to get
supplies, then we go to the Utilidor.

423
00:50:11.216 --> 00:50:13.634
But we'll never make it there
without cover.

424
00:50:14.928 --> 00:50:18.597
We get there, we can last the month.

425
00:50:19.266 --> 00:50:21.809
The next blizzard, we'll be ready.

426
00:50:31.695 --> 00:50:33.612
Hello!

427
00:50:35.073 --> 00:50:37.074
Somebody!

428
00:50:43.040 --> 00:50:45.291
Help!

429
00:50:46.084 --> 00:50:47.960
Come on.

430
00:50:49.880 --> 00:50:52.089
Help!

431
00:50:53.592 --> 00:50:55.760
Please!

432
00:50:56.887 --> 00:50:58.929
Anyone?

433
00:51:00.807 --> 00:51:02.683
Hello?

434
00:51:05.353 --> 00:51:07.396
Anyone?

435
00:51:08.106 --> 00:51:10.107
Help!

436
00:51:13.612 --> 00:51:15.613
We need to get her in
before they find her.

437
00:51:15.781 --> 00:51:17.531
- Wait.
- What?

438
00:51:17.949 --> 00:51:20.618
Look at the rooftops behind her.

439
00:51:25.749 --> 00:51:28.250
Please!

440
00:51:32.130 --> 00:51:34.465
They're using her as bait.

441
00:52:03.161 --> 00:52:04.620
Please.

442
00:52:05.872 --> 00:52:08.332
Please, no. I tried.

443
00:52:08.500 --> 00:52:10.292
There isn't anybody left.

444
00:52:16.133 --> 00:52:17.967
Please.

445
00:52:19.052 --> 00:52:22.429
Please, God. Please.

446
00:52:23.598 --> 00:52:25.808
God?

447
00:52:42.659 --> 00:52:43.951
No God.

448
00:53:03.430 --> 00:53:04.680
Eben.

449
00:53:13.315 --> 00:53:14.940
Eben!

450
00:53:22.032 --> 00:53:23.490
I'll come to you.

451
00:54:05.951 --> 00:54:08.702
I've known Kirsten my whole life.

452
00:54:09.204 --> 00:54:10.246
I'm going out.

453
00:54:10.413 --> 00:54:12.331
Why we waiting?
While they're feeding...

454
00:54:12.499 --> 00:54:14.583
...we could make a run for it.

455
00:54:14.751 --> 00:54:17.294
- I can kill these things.
- We'll die in here otherwise.

456
00:54:17.462 --> 00:54:19.255
Eben doesn't know what he's doing!

457
00:54:19.422 --> 00:54:20.422
- Just move.
- Beau.

458
00:54:20.590 --> 00:54:22.675
We agreed to keep
the bigger weapon here.

459
00:54:22.842 --> 00:54:25.344
- Just move!
- We need you here.

460
00:54:35.814 --> 00:54:37.481
Okay.

461
00:54:37.691 --> 00:54:39.733
Okay. Okay.

462
00:54:51.162 --> 00:54:52.746
John.

463
00:54:54.165 --> 00:54:56.333
How long have you been under there?

464
00:54:57.335 --> 00:54:58.585
I'm not sure.

465
00:54:59.129 --> 00:55:00.671
Where's Ally?

466
00:55:01.798 --> 00:55:04.008
Took Ally.

467
00:55:04.175 --> 00:55:05.968
Couldn't follow.

468
00:55:07.137 --> 00:55:08.846
You're okay?

469
00:55:10.974 --> 00:55:14.393
- The leg hurts.
- Okay.

470
00:55:15.520 --> 00:55:18.314
I know a safe place.

471
00:55:18.481 --> 00:55:22.276
I'm gonna pull you out.
But stay quiet.

472
00:55:24.404 --> 00:55:26.030
Come on.

473
00:55:28.199 --> 00:55:30.200
So hungry.

474
00:55:30.869 --> 00:55:33.662
Yeah, we'll get you
something to eat. Yeah.

475
00:55:40.545 --> 00:55:42.254
What happened to you?

476
00:55:43.256 --> 00:55:44.715
Shit!

477
00:55:53.266 --> 00:55:54.892
Eben.

478
00:55:56.061 --> 00:55:57.227
Come on.

479
00:56:01.608 --> 00:56:03.400
John.

480
00:56:10.909 --> 00:56:14.036
John! Stay back! Stay back!

481
00:56:17.374 --> 00:56:18.582
John.

482
00:56:19.918 --> 00:56:21.293
Stay back!

483
00:57:18.101 --> 00:57:19.685
Are you hurt?

484
00:57:19.894 --> 00:57:21.979
- There's blood.
- He can't breathe.

485
00:57:22.147 --> 00:57:24.148
I'm okay. I'm okay.

486
00:57:24.357 --> 00:57:26.316
Where's your inhaler?

487
00:57:27.652 --> 00:57:30.487
- I lost it.
- Oh, shit.

488
00:57:37.495 --> 00:57:39.913
John Riis became one of them.

489
00:58:37.639 --> 00:58:38.972
Isaac.

490
00:58:43.561 --> 00:58:46.146
No. Isaac.

491
00:58:46.356 --> 00:58:48.649
I'm walking to Wainwright.

492
00:58:48.942 --> 00:58:51.109
It's 80 miles.
There's no way to get there.

493
00:58:52.403 --> 00:58:54.613
- Just go back upstairs.
- Wilson.

494
00:58:54.781 --> 00:58:57.991
Come on down. We need to get
out of here. Bring your mother too.

495
00:58:58.159 --> 00:59:00.744
- Okay, we'll die if you go out there.
- No!

496
00:59:00.912 --> 00:59:05.082
No. I'll die if I stay here. That's what's
gonna happen. Leave me alone.

497
00:59:06.584 --> 00:59:07.709
What's she doing?

498
00:59:08.253 --> 00:59:10.754
Just... Just keep quiet.

499
00:59:12.924 --> 00:59:15.300
- I'm sorry.
- It's all right.

500
00:59:19.097 --> 00:59:21.098
Let's just go back upstairs.

501
00:59:21.266 --> 00:59:23.600
Can I... ? There's a bathroom?

502
00:59:24.269 --> 00:59:26.478
No... Okay, remember
you can't flush.

503
00:59:26.646 --> 00:59:29.022
We'll just open the valve afterwards.

504
00:59:50.461 --> 00:59:53.297
Who would have thought
we'd make it this long, huh?

505
00:59:53.464 --> 00:59:54.798
We're ahead of the curve.

506
00:59:54.966 --> 00:59:57.718
Every day they need more food.
They'll be back.

507
01:00:03.099 --> 01:00:05.642
Dad? Dad?

508
01:00:05.810 --> 01:00:07.311
Dad!

509
01:00:08.104 --> 01:00:09.479
No noise!

510
01:00:17.989 --> 01:00:20.407
- Wait! You can't just rush out.
- He's my father.

511
01:00:20.700 --> 01:00:22.075
Wait! No!

512
01:00:50.438 --> 01:00:52.898
Stella, are you all right?
What happened?

513
01:00:53.066 --> 01:00:56.026
Isaac went to Wainwright.

514
01:00:56.861 --> 01:01:00.447
- Wilson went to find him.
- How long you been down here?

515
01:01:32.980 --> 01:02:15.355
Dad!

516
01:02:53.144 --> 01:02:55.353
I should've fought harder.

517
01:02:57.648 --> 01:02:59.733
Kept Wilson here.

518
01:03:02.236 --> 01:03:05.655
It's hard to stop someone
when their family's at stake.

519
01:03:09.327 --> 01:03:11.536
The things you'll do to save your own.

520
01:03:13.498 --> 01:03:15.749
We were like that once.

521
01:03:17.502 --> 01:03:19.252
Weren't we?

522
01:03:59.377 --> 01:04:01.086
It's gone.

523
01:04:03.548 --> 01:04:04.923
It's snowing.

524
01:04:05.716 --> 01:04:08.385
As soon as it's safe, we have to move.

525
01:05:25.463 --> 01:05:27.422
You four, canned goods.

526
01:05:27.632 --> 01:05:30.550
Stella, Carter, propane, batteries.

527
01:05:30.718 --> 01:05:34.930
Jake, medical supplies. We meet
back here in two minutes. Let's go.

528
01:06:01.332 --> 01:06:04.668
I promised my wife I wouldn't live
on these things while she was gone.

529
01:06:04.835 --> 01:06:06.252
She'll cut you slack.

530
01:06:31.821 --> 01:06:33.697
Oh, God.

531
01:06:37.702 --> 01:06:40.203
I'm done playing with this one.

532
01:06:41.706 --> 01:06:43.748
You wanna play with me now?

533
01:06:45.334 --> 01:06:46.668
Come on!

534
01:06:52.008 --> 01:06:53.049
What?

535
01:06:55.177 --> 01:06:57.053
Okay.

536
01:06:57.888 --> 01:06:59.347
Wait.

537
01:07:55.696 --> 01:07:57.238
Somebody!

538
01:07:57.448 --> 01:07:59.199
Somebody get the ax!

539
01:08:16.717 --> 01:08:18.927
She was just a girl.

540
01:08:24.517 --> 01:08:26.518
You did the right thing.

541
01:08:35.319 --> 01:08:36.653
It's okay.

542
01:08:49.166 --> 01:08:50.792
Who was she?

543
01:08:51.961 --> 01:08:54.254
I mean, does anybody recognize her?

544
01:08:54.713 --> 01:08:57.841
No.

545
01:09:01.345 --> 01:09:03.138
The whiteout's over.

546
01:09:14.108 --> 01:09:16.359
We have to move.

547
01:09:16.527 --> 01:09:18.653
We can't stay here.

548
01:09:18.821 --> 01:09:21.281
But the Utilidor's too far
without cover.

549
01:09:26.704 --> 01:09:27.787
Eben?

550
01:09:28.330 --> 01:09:33.418
Could we make it to your station
if somebody created a diversion?

551
01:09:38.090 --> 01:09:39.215
How?

552
01:09:42.636 --> 01:09:45.096
These things can't survive the sun.

553
01:09:45.848 --> 01:09:47.932
What if we brought the sun early?

554
01:09:50.060 --> 01:09:51.853
Helen had that operation at home.

555
01:09:52.188 --> 01:09:55.273
Yeah. She used an ultraviolet light
to grow the stuff.

556
01:09:55.441 --> 01:09:59.277
Yeah. I can run for her place,
let them follow me.

557
01:09:59.445 --> 01:10:03.072
Hit them with the sun lamp while the
rest of you go to the sheriff's station.

558
01:10:03.240 --> 01:10:05.283
Just because something
stopped Bela Lugosi...

559
01:10:05.451 --> 01:10:08.203
...doesn't mean it can stop
these things.

560
01:10:08.370 --> 01:10:11.581
Why would they send that stranger
to cut us off...

561
01:10:11.749 --> 01:10:13.958
...if they can handle the light?

562
01:10:14.543 --> 01:10:16.461
What if it doesn't work?

563
01:10:20.507 --> 01:10:22.258
It has to.

564
01:10:28.682 --> 01:10:30.308
I'll do it.

565
01:10:31.435 --> 01:10:33.436
- I'm the fastest.
- Bullshit.

566
01:10:34.438 --> 01:10:36.689
I weigh less than you
and I know Grandma's house.

567
01:10:36.857 --> 01:10:40.443
- You're 15 years old. Forget about it.
- I'm 15. Right.

568
01:10:40.611 --> 01:10:43.321
- You've got a wife. People need you.
- Jake.

569
01:10:44.156 --> 01:10:46.324
I saw you in the back with the ax.

570
01:10:47.826 --> 01:10:50.662
You think you're up to doing that
three or four more times?

571
01:10:51.789 --> 01:10:54.249
You don't even think
this plan'll work.

572
01:10:54.458 --> 01:10:56.167
Yeah, but you do.

573
01:10:58.128 --> 01:10:59.462
I'm going.

574
01:11:00.047 --> 01:11:01.965
I'll see you at the station.

575
01:11:02.424 --> 01:11:04.968
You'll need to start her genny first.

576
01:11:07.054 --> 01:11:08.429
See you soon.

577
01:11:17.398 --> 01:11:19.440
Hey!

578
01:11:34.999 --> 01:11:37.208
- Come on.
- Go, go, go.

579
01:11:42.131 --> 01:11:43.548
Hey!

580
01:11:44.258 --> 01:11:46.509
Come on, motherfuckers!

581
01:11:49.513 --> 01:11:50.638
Hey!

582
01:12:19.335 --> 01:12:21.794
Come on. Come on.

583
01:12:52.701 --> 01:12:54.035
Come on!

584
01:13:13.347 --> 01:13:15.181
Let me check.

585
01:13:19.853 --> 01:13:22.021
Okay, quick. Come in.

586
01:13:25.317 --> 01:13:26.401
Come on, Stella.

587
01:14:37.681 --> 01:14:39.348
You there?

588
01:14:41.351 --> 01:14:44.812
Yeah. Yeah, it worked.

589
01:14:45.314 --> 01:14:47.899
But they're gonna cut off
the power, so...

590
01:15:21.558 --> 01:15:24.894
Stella. I got out.

591
01:15:25.687 --> 01:15:28.189
It's good to hear your voice.

592
01:15:28.357 --> 01:15:30.066
Don't wait for me.

593
01:15:32.277 --> 01:15:33.778
Please.

594
01:15:37.032 --> 01:15:38.574
Eben.

595
01:15:40.118 --> 01:15:44.664
Run for Rogers Avenue,
towards the trencher.

596
01:15:49.586 --> 01:15:51.420
It's my turn.

597
01:16:19.658 --> 01:16:21.409
You do understand?

598
01:16:23.704 --> 01:16:29.000
What can be broken must be broken.

599
01:16:51.231 --> 01:16:52.315
Fuck off!

600
01:17:39.738 --> 01:17:42.782
Welcome to Barrow, top of the world.

601
01:18:34.418 --> 01:18:36.711
You ain't gonna eat me.

602
01:19:16.001 --> 01:19:18.794
When a man meets a force...

603
01:19:19.379 --> 01:19:21.672
...he can't destroy...

604
01:19:23.049 --> 01:19:26.469
...he destroys himself instead.

605
01:19:29.014 --> 01:19:31.474
What a plague you are.

606
01:19:57.793 --> 01:19:59.084
Beau...

607
01:20:01.004 --> 01:20:02.838
And Doug.

608
01:20:31.535 --> 01:20:33.744
Now there's six of us.

609
01:20:36.206 --> 01:20:38.332
Soon there'll be just five.

610
01:20:46.383 --> 01:20:49.635
The little girl in the store.

611
01:20:50.595 --> 01:20:52.596
I changed.

612
01:20:53.974 --> 01:20:55.599
I'm just so thirsty now.

613
01:21:01.648 --> 01:21:03.858
I couldn't tell you.

614
01:21:04.401 --> 01:21:08.654
That photo's all I've got left
of my family.

615
01:21:12.284 --> 01:21:15.578
Martha was taking the kids
to visit her mom.

616
01:21:17.664 --> 01:21:19.540
They were hit...

617
01:21:21.084 --> 01:21:23.252
...by a drunk driver.

618
01:21:27.924 --> 01:21:31.635
I wanted to be with them so much.

619
01:21:35.932 --> 01:21:39.393
I couldn't bring myself to do it.

620
01:21:43.231 --> 01:21:46.567
But I know they're waiting for me.

621
01:21:50.614 --> 01:21:54.658
I can't live forever.

622
01:21:55.368 --> 01:21:57.244
I can't.

623
01:21:59.664 --> 01:22:00.706
Eben.

624
01:22:03.668 --> 01:22:05.502
Don't let me.

625
01:22:08.840 --> 01:22:10.674
No, Carter.

626
01:22:11.551 --> 01:22:13.677
He told us what he wants.

627
01:23:38.179 --> 01:23:39.930
Did you see that?

628
01:23:40.432 --> 01:23:41.932
Yeah.

629
01:23:49.733 --> 01:23:51.275
It's Billy.

630
01:24:18.428 --> 01:24:19.928
Billy.

631
01:24:50.293 --> 01:24:52.211
It's Peggy and the girls.

632
01:24:54.798 --> 01:24:57.257
I heard the screams.

633
01:24:58.843 --> 01:25:01.637
I didn't want them to die
like the rest.

634
01:25:03.848 --> 01:25:06.433
I tried to shoot myself too.

635
01:25:06.601 --> 01:25:09.144
The fucking gun jammed.

636
01:25:15.151 --> 01:25:17.027
I shouldn't have signaled to you.

637
01:25:18.863 --> 01:25:21.115
I just couldn't stand being on my own.

638
01:25:40.844 --> 01:25:42.594
You have a family.

639
01:25:45.056 --> 01:25:47.391
You don't ever hurt them!

640
01:25:48.685 --> 01:25:51.854
Don't ever hurt them.

641
01:26:10.874 --> 01:26:13.167
Maybe they tried for the Utilidor.

642
01:27:01.925 --> 01:27:05.928
Gail.

643
01:27:09.724 --> 01:27:10.974
No. Stella.

644
01:27:16.564 --> 01:27:17.940
Stella.

645
01:27:25.615 --> 01:27:27.282
I'll meet you at the Utilidor.

646
01:27:34.958 --> 01:27:37.084
No, Billy, stay there!

647
01:29:15.058 --> 01:29:16.433
Eben!

648
01:29:17.560 --> 01:29:22.731
Jake.

649
01:29:29.781 --> 01:29:31.031
Stella?

650
01:29:32.700 --> 01:29:34.618
Gail Robbins?

651
01:29:35.119 --> 01:29:36.495
We don't know.

652
01:29:50.093 --> 01:29:54.596
It took centuries for us...

653
01:29:54.931 --> 01:29:56.765
...to make them believe...

654
01:29:59.811 --> 01:30:05.482
...we were only bad dreams.

655
01:30:09.654 --> 01:30:16.368
We cannot give them reason to suspect.

656
01:30:17.495 --> 01:30:19.454
Destroy them all.

657
01:31:18.097 --> 01:31:20.599
Stella, this is Eben. Come in.

658
01:31:22.310 --> 01:31:24.019
Where are you?

659
01:31:29.484 --> 01:31:31.234
Hello?

660
01:31:36.908 --> 01:31:40.118
- Hello?
- Stella. This is Eben.

661
01:31:40.286 --> 01:31:42.787
- Come in.
- Anyone?

662
01:32:08.439 --> 01:32:09.689
Eben!

663
01:32:42.223 --> 01:32:44.474
Billy. Bill, hey. Billy!

664
01:32:46.143 --> 01:32:48.270
- Go!
- No. Billy.

665
01:32:48.771 --> 01:32:49.896
Shit. Shit.

666
01:32:57.280 --> 01:32:58.280
Eben!

667
01:33:52.084 --> 01:33:53.460
Hey.

668
01:33:54.837 --> 01:33:57.213
I found these behind Carter's desk.

669
01:33:57.381 --> 01:34:00.508
Chocolates, vitamins and vodka.

670
01:34:03.012 --> 01:34:04.596
Stella, come in. This is Eben.

671
01:34:06.098 --> 01:34:07.891
We should celebrate.

672
01:34:09.727 --> 01:34:11.895
One day till sunrise.

673
01:34:22.823 --> 01:34:25.450
You did good getting everybody here.

674
01:34:33.959 --> 01:34:35.502
Eben.

675
01:34:38.923 --> 01:34:40.715
Stella.

676
01:34:41.050 --> 01:34:44.719
Whisper. They're walking around.

677
01:34:44.929 --> 01:34:48.932
I just had to hear your voice.
I've got Gail with me.

678
01:34:49.100 --> 01:34:50.558
Where are you?

679
01:34:50.726 --> 01:34:53.561
Opposite the Melanson's,
under a wreck.

680
01:35:04.740 --> 01:35:08.410
- Are you okay?
- It's so cold.

681
01:35:08.911 --> 01:35:10.578
We're freezing, Eben.

682
01:35:11.539 --> 01:35:14.916
I can see the car.
The wreck on the right.

683
01:35:16.460 --> 01:35:18.336
We're coming to get you.

684
01:35:21.841 --> 01:35:23.967
There's way too many of them.

685
01:35:24.135 --> 01:35:26.720
They'd kill us before we got to her.

686
01:35:36.105 --> 01:35:38.648
We have to cut off
or they'll hear you.

687
01:35:40.067 --> 01:35:42.694
I'll call you back when it's safe.

688
01:35:46.115 --> 01:35:48.742
The sun comes up tomorrow.

689
01:35:50.119 --> 01:35:52.495
We're gonna watch it together.

690
01:35:54.749 --> 01:35:56.583
I'm so sorry, baby.

691
01:35:58.461 --> 01:36:01.129
I should never have left you.

692
01:36:05.134 --> 01:36:07.844
The street's filling up with oil.

693
01:36:14.935 --> 01:36:17.270
They broke into the pipeline.

694
01:36:47.009 --> 01:36:49.177
They're burning down the town.

695
01:37:05.277 --> 01:37:07.695
Nobody will know what happened.

696
01:37:09.365 --> 01:37:11.950
They'll just think it was
some horrible accident.

697
01:37:18.290 --> 01:37:21.709
Next time they'll take out
Point Hope, Wainwright.

698
01:37:27.216 --> 01:37:29.175
Wait. Wait.

699
01:37:29.677 --> 01:37:32.971
This building's strong.
Can't we just ride it out here?

700
01:37:43.816 --> 01:37:45.859
He'll kill her if she runs.

701
01:37:48.821 --> 01:37:50.363
She'll burn if she stays.

702
01:37:55.578 --> 01:37:58.371
You go out there,
won't they come after all of us?

703
01:38:11.927 --> 01:38:13.219
Oh, dear God.

704
01:38:13.762 --> 01:38:15.430
Eben.

705
01:38:21.896 --> 01:38:23.438
Eben!

706
01:38:28.152 --> 01:38:29.527
Eben.

707
01:38:31.030 --> 01:38:32.655
Jake...

708
01:38:32.823 --> 01:38:36.117
...when they're all watching me,
get on the walkie-talkie...

709
01:38:38.162 --> 01:38:42.540
...and tell Stella to run for it.
-What are you talking about?

710
01:38:48.005 --> 01:38:49.631
Eben.

711
01:38:50.591 --> 01:38:55.136
When John Riis and Carter changed,
they were only bitten.

712
01:38:55.304 --> 01:38:57.805
They stayed who they were
for a little while.

713
01:39:00.809 --> 01:39:03.227
We can't fight them
the way that we are.

714
01:39:07.942 --> 01:39:09.984
Thanks, little brother.

715
01:39:12.446 --> 01:39:14.447
Take care of Stella for me.

716
01:39:20.788 --> 01:39:23.957
- Are you fucking crazy?
- It's somebody else's blood.

717
01:39:45.896 --> 01:39:50.608
- He's one of them.
- How do we know he won't attack us?

718
01:39:51.151 --> 01:39:54.278
- Maybe we should stop him now.
- Shut up.

719
01:39:54.446 --> 01:39:55.822
Shut up!

720
01:39:58.409 --> 01:40:00.410
Nobody touches him.

721
01:40:06.250 --> 01:40:08.042
I can smell your blood.

722
01:40:28.647 --> 01:40:31.232
You can't fight them all, Eben.

723
01:41:15.903 --> 01:41:17.779
Stella, it's Jake.

724
01:41:18.906 --> 01:41:20.948
Get out of there now. Run.

725
01:41:27.623 --> 01:41:29.290
The one who fights.

726
01:42:23.554 --> 01:42:25.096
Go!

727
01:44:29.805 --> 01:44:32.306
What did you do to yourself?

728
01:44:33.558 --> 01:44:35.643
What I had to.

729
01:44:39.314 --> 01:44:40.773
Should I go after them?

730
01:44:47.364 --> 01:44:51.993
- It's almost dawn. We made it.
- Eben.

731
01:44:52.494 --> 01:44:54.287
The dawn.
